    "path": "sources/treasury-mts/mts-202605.pdf",
    "table": "Table 5. Outlays of the U.S. Government, May 2026 and Other Periods",
    "page": 14,
    "title": "Department of Homeland Security section (Table-5 cap-fit unit, page 14). Full 9-column outlays model. Reclassified from over-cap to cap-fit by the 2026-07-15 sizing pass (126 cells). NESTED (family 3): Federal Emergency Management Agency rolls Disaster Relief + National Flood Insurance Fund + Other into Total--FEMA, which then feeds the department roll-up. FEMA's Applicable column is single-source (only National Flood Insurance Fund carries an applicable), so the Total--FEMA applicable subtotal is a leaf covered by the FEMA total-row net identity (-state / plan Pattern addendum). Family pattern: plans/treasury-mts-2026-05-outlays-table5.md; worked examples: -state (nesting + single-source), -commerce (flat).",
    "period": "May FY2026 (This Month = May 2026; Current FYTD = Oct 2025 - May 2026; Prior FYTD = Oct 2024 - May 2025)"
  },
  "unit_note": "USD millions ('[$ millions]' per table header). Table 5 legend (p. 23): '......' = 'No Transactions' (omitted); '(**)' = 'Less than absolute value of $500,000' (none in this section). Values as printed, thousands separators stripped, negatives as leading '-'. Nine-column model: 3 periods x (Gross Outlays / Applicable Receipts / Outlays[net]). FEMA nests (family 3); its Applicable column has a single contributing line (National Flood Insurance Fund), so the FEMA gross/net columns roll up but the FEMA Applicable column does not -- the Total--FEMA applicable cells (c2/c5/c8) are marked leaf and covered by the FEMA total-row net identity, while the National Flood Insurance Fund line-level applicable is covered by its own per-line net identity. At the department level the Applicable column has four sources (Customs and Border Protection, Total--FEMA, Proprietary, Offsetting), so it rolls up normally. Non-default tolerances quote the Table-5 rounding note (p. 23): 'Note: Details may not add to totals due to rounding.' The department PFYTD Gross roll-up (col 7) is off by 3 -- the largest gap here -- across 13 independently-rounded sources; within the plan's sanctioned +/-1..3 band, all 13 render-verified.",
